# What `railway up` must not upload. Everything here is also in .dockerignore; this file exists
# because .dockerignore is applied by the builder, after the CLI has already sent the bytes.
#
# assets/ is README media (a 21 MB demo.mp4 and an 11 MB demo.gif) rendered by GitHub, never by the
# app — there is no public/ dir and no code path references it. It was 32 MB of a 35 MB upload, and
# large uploads were failing mid-flight on this link ("received fatal alert: BadRecordMac", then
# "Broken pipe"), which blocked deploying at all. Nothing in the image needs it.
assets

node_modules
.next
.git
.env
.env.*
*.log
.DS_Store
.notes
dist
out
coverage

